        # ---- Nature & Scope of Economics (7)
        R1("Scarcity in economics means that", "resources are limited while human wants are unlimited",
           ["there is no money in the economy", "goods are too expensive for the poor", "wants are limited while resources are unlimited"],
           ["Scarcity is about resources and wants, not only about money.", "Scarcity applies to rich and poor alike.", "This reverses the idea."],
           "Scarcity arises because resources cannot satisfy all wants.", T1, "Recall", "Compare resources with wants."),
        R1("A farmer plants maize on a plot. Beans would have earned FCFA 80 000 and cassava FCFA 60 000 on the same plot. The opportunity cost of growing maize is",
           "the FCFA 80 000 that beans would have earned",
           ["FCFA 140 000, the total of both alternatives", "FCFA 60 000, the cassava income", "the cost of the maize seed"],
           ["Only the next best alternative is the opportunity cost, not all alternatives.", "Cassava is not the next best alternative.", "Seed cost is a money cost, not the opportunity cost."],
           "Opportunity cost is the value of the best alternative given up.", T1, "Application", "Which alternative is the best one given up?"),
        R1("A point inside a production possibility curve shows that", "resources are not fully used",
           ["the economy is growing", "the output is impossible", "all resources are fully employed"],
           ["Growth is shown by a shift of the curve.", "Impossible output lies outside the curve.", "Full use is shown by a point on the curve."],
           "Points inside the curve mean idle or inefficiently used resources.", T2, "Concept", "Where do fully used resources lie?"),
